# Django Models Rule

- Domain entities must inherit from the shared audited base model.
- Avoid `QuerySet.update()` and `bulk_update()` for audited entities because they bypass audit events.
- Use cancel/status transitions instead of hard delete where the specification requires `CANCEL`.
- `Person` identity-linked fixed fields are immutable per identity number unless changed through an explicit correction workflow that is audited.
- Every schema change must include migration files and related requirements document updates.
